#POISSON PROCESS DISTRIBUTION BASED SPIKE GENERATOR

# Poisson distribution - memoryless (doesnt depend on past events) time dependent series of event.
# Chance of an event depends on rate λ(t).
# Chance for an event to occur in a deltat timeframe = deltat * λ(t)
# Fishing in a pond - chances diminish from successful fishing iteration to the other - not poisson
# Fishing in the sea - chances remain the same between iterations - poisson
# Homogenous poisson - rate λ is constant --> If theres a refractory period the rate is not constant in time
# Inhomogenous poisson process - has refractory period --> time varying (varying rate)
# For homogenous poisson --> the distribution of the inter-event(inter-spike) intervals is an exponential distribution: p(t) = lambda / e^(lambdat)
# Fano factor measures variability of dataset: F = Variance / Avg in homogenous = 1
# Coefficient of variation usually applied to ISI: Cv = Variance / Avg in homogenous = 1

